{"agent_id":"pp3g-zpjP-audit-read-only-flag-only-independently-verify-the","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-18T06:52:27.653232615Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b3f17d6f-b76e-4208-9373-d4cf3b99c0b3","comment_uuid":"15c5c5eb-2e7d-4081-8dfb-9a155d1cbac5","author":"pp3g-zpjP-audit-read-only-flag-only-independently-verify-the","content":"## Audit Verdict: CONDITIONAL PASS\n\n**Auditor:** mimo-v2.5 (opencode-go/mimo-v2.5) | **Commit:** 41c1936a | **File:** .crosslink/knowledge/model-discipline.md | **Date:** 2026-08-18\n\n### Architectural Assessment\n\n- [OK] — Standing Facts section inserted after Mandatory Rules (lines 28-37), correct placement in document hierarchy. Section header matches the operator-stated convention from issue #400.\n- [OK] — Frontmatter updated field set to 2026-08-18 (line 2). Matches commit date and issue creation date.\n- [OK] — Single-file change (.crosslink/knowledge/model-discipline.md only), no unintended side effects.\n\n### Standing Facts — Accuracy Verification (against operator statements in #400)\n\n- [OK] — **Fact #1 (line 30):** 'Only OpenCode credits exist — NO OpenRouter credits.' Accurately captures the operator's stated constraint. The parenthetical 'unless the operator explicitly states otherwise' provides a correct escape hatch.\n- [OK] — **Fact #2 (line 32):** 'Google models are always served from Vertex AI (prefix google-vertex/).' Accurate. Internally consistent: the Google Vertex AI section (lines 112-114) correctly uses the google-vertex/ prefix on all three listed models.\n- [OK] — **Fact #3 (line 34):** 'Website NEVER displays full model IDs. Zen catalog API is authority.' Accurate. The Zen API URL (https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/models) matches the Provider Links section (line 105). The agent-scoped task description is correct — builders must query the API themselves.\n\n### Consistency with Rest of Page\n\n- [OK] — Fact #2's reference to 'The Google Vertex AI section' resolves correctly to lines 108-114. The section exists and uses the google-vertex/ prefix as stated.\n- [OK] — No contradiction with the Go vs Zen table (lines 9-15): the table describes cost/reliability profiles; the Standing Facts describe provider availability constraints. Complementary, not conflicting.\n- [OK] — Fact #1 does not conflict with the whitelist (lines 97-105): the whitelist enumerates opencode/ (Zen free) models, which are OpenCode providers — in scope per fact #1.\n- [OK] — Fact #3 is consistent with Mandatory Rule #1 (line 18): 'Always verify with opencode models' — both agree the local cache is the first check, and fact #3补充 that when the cache is stale, the Zen API is the fallback.\n\n### models.dev-lag Note Verification\n\n- [OK] — The NOTE (line 36) states models.dev lags behind the Zen API. Confirmed by issue #399 findings: local 'opencode models opencode' returned only 5 models vs 62 from the Zen API. The lag is real and significant. The note's wording ('Absence of a model from opencode models output does NOT mean the model is unavailable on Zen') is accurate and important.\n\n### Cross-reference with Issue #399 (Zen API Findings)\n\n- [OK] — The Standing Facts do not contradict the #399 findings. The Zen API confirmed 62 free models and 26 Go models — the facts correctly state the API is the authority over the local cache.\n- [OK] — The 'agent-scoped task' characterization of querying the Zen API is consistent with #399's finding that the API returns valid JSON without authentication.\n\n### Pre-existing Issues (NOT introduced by this commit — flagged for awareness)\n\n- [CONCERN] — **Whitelist staleness (lines 97-105):** The whitelist lists 7 models (big-pickle, deepseek-v4-flash-free, laguna-s-2.1-free, ling-3.0-flash-free, mimo-v2.5-free, nemotron-3-ultra-free, north-mini-code-free). The Zen API from #399 shows additional free models (hy3-free, nemotron-3.5-lightning-free) that are NOT in the whitelist. This is pre-existing drift, not introduced by the Standing Facts commit, but it means the whitelist section contradicts the NOTE's message that the API is authoritative.\n- [CONCERN] — **Google Vertex section staleness (lines 112-114):** Lists gemini-3.1-pro-preview, gemini-3.5-flash, gemini-2.5-pro. The Zen API from #399 shows gemini-3.7-flash exists but is absent here. Pre-existing, not introduced by this commit.\n- [CONCERN] — **OpenCode Go section staleness (lines 88-94):** Lists 6 models. The Zen Go API from #399 shows 26 models total — significantly more are available. Pre-existing.\n- [CONCERN] — **OpenCode Zen section staleness (lines 96-105):** The whitelist note says 'Paid Zen models are not exposed because no Zen API credits are used' — this is consistent with fact #1 (no credits). However, the section header says '(whitelist, issue #103)' which references an old issue, and the actual model list has drifted from the Zen API.\n\n### Process Assessment\n\n- [OK] — Builder's plan comment on #400 accurately described the intended change.\n- [OK] — Builder's result comment on #400 accurately described what was done.\n- [OK] — Commit message matches the change (conventional commit style, issue reference).\n- [OK] — Single-file, focused change. No scope creep.\n- [CONCERN] — Builder's handoff note says 'All other content unchanged' — this is true for this commit, but the pre-existing staleness in other sections means the page as a whole has drift that the Standing Facts section's own message (API is authoritative) implicitly highlights.\n\n### Systemic Risks Identified\n\n- **Risk:** The Standing Facts section's message ('query the Zen API, the local cache lags') creates an implicit expectation that other sections should reflect current API data. The pre-existing staleness in whitelist, Google Vertex, and Go sections now contradicts this message. **Impact:** Agents following the new Standing Facts guidance will discover the documented model lists are incomplete. **Mitigation:** A follow-up issue to reconcile the Currently Verified Models section with the Zen API data from #399.\n- **Risk:** The whitelist section (lines 97-105) claims models are 'whitelisted to exactly these free models in plugin.ts and dynamic-models.ts' — if the actual plugin code has been updated to include hy3-free or others, the documentation is wrong. **Impact:** Agents may attempt to use models that are blocked by the plugin, or ignore models that are actually available. **Mitigation:** Verify plugin.ts/dynamic-models.ts against the whitelist and reconcile.\n\n### Recommendations\n\n1. **File a follow-up issue** to reconcile Currently Verified Models and whitelist sections with Zen API data from #399. Priority: medium. Rationale: the Standing Facts section's own guidance (API is authoritative) makes the stale sections increasingly confusing.\n2. **No corrections needed** to the Standing Facts section itself. The three facts, the NOTE, and the frontmatter update are all accurate and consistent.\n\n### Preconditions for Full PASS\n\n1. The Standing Facts section content is accurate and requires no corrections — **MET**.\n2. The models.dev-lag note is accurate — **MET**.\n3. Frontmatter updated field is 2026-08-18 — **MET**.\n4. No contradictions with the rest of the page — **MET** (pre-existing drift in other sections is not a contradiction with the new content).\n\n**Verdict stands: CONDITIONAL PASS.** The Standing Facts section is correct as written. The pre-existing staleness in surrounding sections is a systemic issue that predates this commit and should be tracked separately.","created_at":"2026-08-18T06:52:27.645955692Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:D59xp0flCkF+7B9V4H3j69GrK7QXCmZUrhfjSI5ed/I","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgv8Z9t3lmt0Dy3fjeLcQwP3lf2vASkZzo+/1IlBXT9bQAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABADdmlHu7GmKaYInJlWFbm5ZXNHvB8WGA2u8pyN4/J5OBp7lGkXFIZAcMnzlqMjLjSoV0TBB030JU5kr1qm2rBAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:D59xp0flCkF+7B9V4H3j69GrK7QXCmZ